==English==
{{was wotd|2020|December|26}}

===Etymology===
The {{glossary|noun}} is borrowed from {{bor|en|ru|агитпро́п|t=agitprop}}, {{m|ru|Агитпро́п|t=Agitprop (Department for Agitation and Propaganda of the Soviet Union)}}, short for {{m|ru|[[отде́л]] [[агитация|агитации]] [[и]] [[пропаганда|пропаганды]]|t=Department for Agitation and Propaganda}}; analysable as a {{blend|en|agitation|propaganda|nocap=1}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=4018|date=September 2012|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from the noun.

