===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}} {{term-label|en|politics}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|also|attributively}} [[political|Political]] [[propaganda]] [[disseminate]]d through [[art]], [[drama]], [[literature]], etc., especially [[communist]] propaganda; {{lb|en|specifically|communism|historical}} such propaganda formerly disseminated by the Department for Agitation and Propaganda of the {{w|Central Committee of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:John Bolton|chapter=The Singapore Sling|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=QjTMDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT67|title=[[w:The Room Where It Happened|The Room Where It Happened: A White House Memoir]]|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Simon & Schuster|date=23 June 2020|page=96|isbn=978-1-9821-4803-4|passage=The letter was pure puffery, probably written by some clerk in North Korea's '''agitprop''' bureau, but [[w:Donald Trump|[Donald] Trump]] loved it.}}
#* '''2024''', Jeremy B. Rudd, ''A Practical Guide to Macroeconomics, p. 2
#*: Like most pieces of '''agitprop,''' the Lucas and Sargent paper vastly overstated the deficiencies of the old order.
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[instance#Noun|instance]] of such propaganda.
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[organization]] or [[person]] [[engage]]d in disseminating such propaganda.

